  "description": "UJAVUY01 crystallizes in the tetragonal crystal system with space group P -4 21 c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C148 H112 N12 O44 Si1 Tb8. From the CIF bond table, Tb1 (Tb) has 6 O neighbors; Tb2 (Tb) has 9 O neighbors; Tb1A (Tb) has 6 O neighbors; Tb2A (Tb) has 9 O neighbors; Tb1F (Tb) has 6 O neighbors; Tb2F (Tb) has 9 O neighbors; Tb1G (Tb) has 6 O neighbors; Tb2G (Tb) has 9 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 14 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.791-4.489 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 102.94-126.79°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Tb8L8(C6H4NH2COO)4SiO4] (C148H112N12O44SiTb8).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
